{
  "category": "Wind Chime Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "CHIMECHO makes its cries echo inside its hollow body. When this POKéMON becomes enraged, its cries result in ultrasonic waves that have the power to knock foes flying.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "In high winds, CHIMECHO cries as it hangs from a tree branch or the eaves of a building using a suction cup on its head. This POKéMON plucks berries with its long tail and eats them.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "They fly about very actively when the hot season arrives. They communicate among themselves using seven different and distinguishing cries.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It travels by riding on winds. It cleverly uses its long tail to pluck nuts and berries, which it loves to eat.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It travels by riding on winds. It cleverly uses its long tail to pluck nuts and berries, which it loves to eat.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "To knock foes flying, it makes the air shudder with its cries. It converses using seven cries.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "Emitting ultrasonic cries, it floats on winds to travel great distances.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its cries echo inside its hollow body to emerge as beautiful notes for startling and repelling foes.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "It uses the sucker on its head to hang from a tree or from eaves. It can produce seven different tones.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
